{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"14","question_sha256":"c407a98da461df30a13c94b0c6e8997e74951fd18aba2ba17788545c45f681ed","reason":"25% of 80 is 20; after selling 6, 20 - 6 = 14. This unambiguously equals the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6948"},{"independent_answer":"45","question_sha256":"386e89e9880506fd52e6e13a14bc53ed88ad80a5bd5727c06eee877995f6dc9b","reason":"The item-specific discount is 20% of $20 = $4, reducing the $54 cart to $50. The subsequent 10% coupon removes $5, leaving $45, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5861"},{"independent_answer":"19","question_sha256":"55109f9b170b3a6c7d8adf2e76fcb5e83216054ce839cd1880c30ef3d7ddce6d","reason":"50% of 190 fights is 95 knockouts, and 20% of 95 is 19. This equals the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3558"},{"independent_answer":"12000","question_sha256":"b47ae2368cc44c141198126a7233a971dcaecb403cf5618945c9b8db658c6f5b","reason":"There are 150 × 10 = 1500 seats. With 20% untaken, 80% or 1200 seats are sold; 1200 × $10 = $12,000, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6128"},{"independent_answer":"19","question_sha256":"19d53bd79d8b622d7cfdae8d207117ee4dd0f6ce61e63ab065076fee5cfa919a","reason":"Kelly's 34 kg is 85% of Megan's weight, so Megan weighs 34/0.85 = 40 kg and Mike weighs 45 kg. Their total is 119 kg, which exceeds 100 kg by 19 kg, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1476"},{"independent_answer":"120","question_sha256":"6fc7de7248295f6f3d73afeec870c1633aaa05f265b1b309649eb2eb0b7f084a","reason":"Wraps add 25% of 600 = 150 pounds, while sleeves add 30 pounds. The extra benefit from wraps is 150 - 30 = 120 pounds, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1065"},{"independent_answer":"2400","question_sha256":"0f86611879e4cc4594c55ec44fca40bc224d208044ced920cff999abdc25cb60","reason":"Because withdrawn interest does not compound, annual interest is $2000 × 0.08 = $160. Over 2.5 years it is $400, and $2000 + $400 = $2400, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-7120"},{"independent_answer":"885000","question_sha256":"1c747b3d9e3053ff62e83e3bbf8be784b0f5b41586acc4df2afd689fca93880c","reason":"Using 52 weeks in a year, James deposits $2000 × 52 = $104,000, producing a $354,000 balance. A windfall worth 50% more than that balance is $531,000; adding it gives $885,000, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1342"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["Next, I calculate how many pits sprout:","80 \\times 0.25 = 20","20 - 6 = 14"],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-6948:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The target relies only on the supplied quantities and explicitly verifiable percentage multiplication and subtraction; it claims no external feedback or checker event.","raw_call_sha256":"f449c7a860876973e5cd5c50eea4d989c318c4d254781186ebf0a83e39ed7538","reason":"The response gives a substantive first-person calculation, correctly finds 20 sprouts and subtracts 6 to obtain 14. Its numerical intermediate is checkable, the percentage-then-subtraction method is reusable, and the text is relevant throughout.","reusable_content":true,"status":"PASS","student_prefix_sha256":"de7abd61344b9421735d9ebbe254dccae029f8d3e940abd85e867babbe2e5392","target_sha256":"fdb373874cfd0cd127586732144492b89b441153deac79c526af7a13a1adc756"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["I first calculated the number of saplings that sprouted.","80 \\times 0.25 = 20","Subtracting 6 from 20 gives 14."],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-6948:new_record","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The record is supported by the question and prior neutral solution. Its verification is described as the writer's own arithmetic check, not an unsupported externa